=== Task 7: Feature Importances & Interpretation ===
--- Feature Importances (Random Forest) ---
  crime_index        0.8898  ###################################
  Hour               0.0514  ##
  District           0.0362  #
  domestic_index     0.0225

--- Interpretation Answers ---
Which feature is most important?
The 'crime_index' is the most important feature.
Does this match the arrest rate analysis from Task 4?
Yes, crime types like NARCOTICS and PROSTITUTION have significantly higher arrest rates compared to others.

Why does Logistic Regression perform worse than tree-based models on this data?
Logistic Regression assumes features contribute linearly. It treats 'crime_index' as an ordered continuous number, which is incorrect for categorical data. Tree models capture non-linear patterns and split correctly on index values.